          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கோல் — kōl — \"a goal in sport\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கடைசி நிமிடத்தில் அவன் ஒரு கோல் போட்டான். kaṭaici nimiṭattil avaṉ oru kōl pōṭṭāṉ. In the last minute he scored a goal."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One scores with போடு (pōṭu) or அடி: கோல் (kōl) போடு. It sounds like the native கோல் (kōl), a stick."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கோல் (kōl) in the sense \"a goal\" is a loan from English goal; it sounds the same as the native கோல் (kōl), \"a stick, a rod\", a different word."
            }
          ]
        },
